<p>You are right, and after making a quick research I found this gloss units are actually used to measure reflective surfaces, apparently a mirror would give around 2000 gloss units at a 20° angle of its surface, the device used to get this measurement is called &quot;gloss meter&quot; so the author if he seems fit, could rephrase &quot;it will seek out the nearest mirror-like surface.&quot; to &quot;it will seek the nearest surface to measure 2000 GU at a 20° angle&quot; or something along those lines, I don't think is a change that is necessary, as it would probably also need a bit of clarification prior to that sentence, like saying it can only be contained on a surface that measure that quantity or similar quantity of gloss units, as I said this is not really necessary, but it would make it look a little more scientific.</p>

							</div>

								
					
